"""The analytical SQL front end: `sql_token` lexes a SQL string into tokens, `sql_parser` parses them into the statement, relation and expression nodes `sql_ast` holds, `sql_fn_table` maps each SQL function name to the expression it lowers to, and `sql_catalog` / `sql_udf_catalog` hold the tables and user functions a query resolves names against, `sql_tvf_bind` gives the `read_csv` / `read_json` / `read_avro` / `read_orc` table functions their bind-time schema and scan leaf, and `sql_frontend` takes SQL text to a bound statement or a query plan (`statement_from_sql`, `plan_from_sql`)."""
